answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "22464"] "category" "local_authored" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/repairs.json" "file_sha256" "0328005daa91919dd8bb81fd729228440954ec812e808e91c99da77efc57aee9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653} {"question" "q-288814" "field" "answer" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "− 22464"] "category" "local_authored" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/repairs.json" "file_sha256" "0328005daa91919dd8bb81fd729228440954ec812e808e91c99da77efc57aee9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653}] "sources" [{"question" "q-98132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the distance between the points $A(-5,2,9)$ and $B(-1,-2,9)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-98132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The distance $d$ between two points $A({x}_{1},{y}_{1},{z}_{1})$ and $B({x}_{2},{y}_{2},{z}_{2})$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $A{{(-5,2,9)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{, }{y}_{1}\\text{, }{z}_{1}\\text{)}}$ and $B{{(-1,-2,9)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{, }{y}_{2}\\text{, }{z}_{2}\\text{)}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(-1-(-5))^{2}+(-2-2)^{2}+(9-9)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{32} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-98132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-98132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-98132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-98132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-112964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the polynomial $f(x)=20{x}^{5}-7{x}^{4}+x-4,$ how many *potential* roots are given by the rational roots theorem?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-112964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $-4,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1,$ $\\pm 2$ and $\\pm 4.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $20,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1,$ $\\pm 2,$ $\\pm 4,$ $\\pm 5,$ $\\pm 10$ and $\\pm 20.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{20}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{2}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{20}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{4}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to the lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{20}, \\\\ \\pm 2, & \\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{10}, \\\\ \\pm 4, & \\pm 2, & \\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{4}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that several potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates, and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{20},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{10},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{5},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{2}{5},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{4}{5},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 4.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $20$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 10=20.$)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-112964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-112964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-112964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "36"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-112964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-113824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}=a$ and $\\frac{12g}{7h}=b,$ what is $a÷b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-113824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute\n\n$$\na÷b=\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}÷\\frac{12g}{7h},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}÷\\frac{12g}{7h} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{7h}{12g} & = \\\\ \\frac{4g\\cdot g}{7h\\cdot {h}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{7h}{3\\cdot 4g} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4g}\\cdot g}{\\cancel{7h}\\cdot {h}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{7h}}{3\\cdot \\cancel{4g}} & = \\\\ \\frac{g}{3{h}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-113824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-113824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-113824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3g}{{h}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{3{h}^{2}}{g}"] ["math" "\\frac{g{h}^{2}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{g}{3{h}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{{g}^{2}}{3h}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-113824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{g}{3{h}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-66428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve  the equation $\\,-{x}^{2}-2x-17=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-66428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=-1,b=-2,$ and $c=-17.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(-1)(-17)}}{2(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{4-68}}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-64}}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}}{-2} \\\\  & =-1\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-1+4\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-1-4\\,\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-66428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-66428" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-66428" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-1\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "x=-1\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "x=-1\\pm \\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "x=-2\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "x=-2\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-66428" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-1\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-69271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Factor the expression ${p}^{4}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-69271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference of squares formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}-{b}^{2}=(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{p}^{4}-1={({p}^{2})}^{2}-{1}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{({p}^{2})}^{2}-{1}^{2}=({p}^{2}+1)({p}^{2}-1)\n$$\n\nFinally, we notice that the expression in the second set of parentheses is also a difference of squares. Therefore, the expression can be factored further, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({p}^{2}+1)({p}^{2}-1) & =({p}^{2}+1)({p}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =({p}^{2}+1)(p+1)(p-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-69271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-69271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-69271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(p+1)^{4}"] ["math" "(p-1)^{4}"] ["math" "({p}^{2}+1)(p+1)(p-1)"] ["math" "({p}^{2}+1)(p+1)^{2}"] ["math" "({p}^{2}+1)(p-1)^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-69271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "({p}^{2}+1)(p+1)(p-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-288814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-5x-14=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the product of its solutions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-288814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=7,\\,b=-5,\\,c=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{a} & =\\frac{(-14)}{7}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-288814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-288814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-288814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{7}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-288814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-71164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-71164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{5+1})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-71164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-71164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-71164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12{x}^{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{12}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{x}^{6}}{12}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{6}}{4}+C"] ["math" "{x}^{6}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-71164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{6}}{4}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-74715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=-3-2\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-74715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/assets/0c6548a95b2a81c7dcde33ead78ee0be8d5cee936edc1e2a98c2d59d259404b7.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\pi <\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ If $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})≈0.588\\,00.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)≈\\pi +0.588\\,00≈3.73\n$$\n\nto two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-74715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-74715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-74715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3.35"] ["math" "3.37"] ["math" "3.53"] ["math" "3.73"] ["math" "7.33"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-74715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3.73"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-338378" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/assets/601562e6fab230b818a1776e42b700518f803f425dcb7f407d3659e91db0ff33.png)\n\nIf the figure above shows the graph of $f(x),$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-338378" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the power and quotient rules, we can rewrite the given limit as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{{({lim}_{x\\to 2}(3f(x)+2))}^{2}}{{({lim}_{x\\to 2}(f(x)-2))}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above is true provided that  ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ exists.\n\nWe find from the graph that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=1.$ We calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(3f(x)+2)=3(1)+2=5\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(f(x)-2)=1-2=-1\n$$\n\nSo we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{25}{-1}=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-338378" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-338378" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-338378" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-122084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Linda wants to buy a refreshing drink. The store has $6$ types of sodas, $6$ types of juices, and $3$ types of water. How many choices of drinks does Linda have?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-122084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to find the total number of choices Linda has, we can use the **rule of sum**:\n\n$$\n6+6+3=15\n$$\n\nTherefore, Linda has $15$ choices of drinks." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-122084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f0ccc31ad821704b8780b3a10eeeab7aff4fd64f71b94dd6e5a65a0c6433e7b"} {"question" "q-122084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6ab6f97a38178aa20d49f423edaa20c88ccbe5d839764d89a180bf5224e4d6a"} {"question" "q-122084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "m